  m_Name: RosettaStone
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Rosetta Stone
  description: The Rosetta Stone is a stone with writing carved into it. There are
    3 types of writing on the Rosetta stone; Greek, Egyptian, and another form of
    Egyptian writing. French soldiers found it in Egypt in 1799. It helped people
    get a better understanding of the Ancient Egyptian writing system called hieroglyphics.
    Its discovery led to the translation of Ancient Egyptian writing. The stone is
    named after the city where it was found, Rosetta (also called Rashid). The stone
    is now in the British Museum in London.
  audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a311eb32799731844ac607f863d5b2a8, type: 3}
